## 2 Elaboration

Elaboration resolves the imports, binds the constants, instantiates every module with its dimensions, and checks shapes, regularity classes and effects. Its output is the program with every instance named and every parameter's shape known.

```text
== ../../examples/spec/mlp/mlp.psk (main)
module Linear{In Out : dim} {
  param w : ℝ[In, Out]  init
  param b : ℝ[Out]  init
  fn apply(x : ℝ[..., In]) -> ℝ[..., Out]
}
module MLP{D hidden : dim} {
  use l1 : Linear{D, hidden}
  use l2 : Linear{hidden, D}
  fn apply(x : ℝ[..., D]) -> ℝ[..., D]
}
fn mse{D : dim}(net : MLP{D, 4*D}, θ : params MLP{D, 4*D}, x : ℝ[batch: B, model: D], y : ℝ[batch: B, model: D]) -> ℝ[]   -- implicit dims: B
fn mse_grad{D : dim}(net : MLP{D, 4*D}, θ : params MLP{D, 4*D}, x : ℝ[batch: B, model: D], y : ℝ[batch: B, model: D]) -> params MLP{D, 4*D}   -- implicit dims: B
== implicit dimensions: B
== instances
Linear{D, hidden}:
  w : ℝ[D, hidden]
  b : ℝ[hidden]
Linear{hidden, D}:
  w : ℝ[hidden, D]
  b : ℝ[D]
MLP{D, 4*D}:
  l1.w : ℝ[D, 4*D]
  l1.b : ℝ[4*D]
  l2.w : ℝ[4*D, D]
  l2.b : ℝ[D]
```

**Types, regularity and effects**, as `presk check --summary` prints them:

